<!-- ════════════════ 52 · THE HONEST NUMBERS ════════════════ -->
  <section data-label="Honest numbers" class="slide light cat-themed" style="--c: #d97706;">
    <div class="glow soft"></div>
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="cat-head">
        <span class="cat-icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10.29 3.86 1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>
        </span>
        <div class="cat-text">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span class="num">52</span>The honest numbers</p>
          <h2 class="h2">AI speeds things up, but <span class="accent">not automatically</span>.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="frame-body">
      <div class="grid-2" style="margin-top: 32px; align-content: start;">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="lab">On scoped work</span>
          <div style="font-size: 96px; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.03em; color: var(--c);">55%</div>
          <p>faster on a scoped task. Copilot users finished the work in 1h11 versus 2h41.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="lab">Where it bites</span>
          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px;">
            <div>
              <div style="font-size: 54px; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--c);">19% slower</div>
              <p style="margin: 4px 0 0;">Experienced devs on their own large, familiar codebase were slower with AI, while sure they were faster.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div style="font-size: 54px; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--c);">~1 in 5</div>
              <p style="margin: 4px 0 0;">packages hallucinated by open-source models (~1 in 20 for commercial). Attackers register the names.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout">
        The same value-per-token curve, now <strong>measured</strong>: AI pays off on small, scoped work and bites in large, familiar code. DORA 2025 calls AI an amplifier, so scope tight and verify the output.
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.45; color: #94a3b8; margin: 14px 4px 0;"><strong>Sources:</strong> GitHub Copilot productivity study (GitHub, 2022) &middot; METR autonomous task study (2025) &middot; Spracklen et al., &ldquo;We Have a Package for You!&rdquo; (USENIX Security 2025): open-source models ~21.7%, commercial ~5.2% package-hallucination rate &middot; DORA State of DevOps 2025.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% set slideNumber = "52" %}
    {% set slideTotal = "57" %}
    {% include "../../shared/chrome.njk" %}
  </section>
